1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,237
ACR stands for Arc Compute Rate. It publishes reference

2
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:09,438
indices for AI inference, GPU compute, and data delivery,

3
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:11,644
with updates recorded on-chain.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,660
Deployed on Arc, ACR's PolicyWallet contract holds

5
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:20,095
a business's USDC, enforces spending limits, and links

6
00:00:19,995 --> 00:00:23,718
each payment to a verifiable record of the decision behind

7
00:00:23,618 --> 00:00:24,298
it.

8
00:00:23,987 --> 00:00:28,255
Aomi combines ACR's internal APIs with the ability

9
00:00:28,155 --> 00:00:31,645
to read its on-chain contracts and prepare transactions

10
00:00:31,545 --> 00:00:34,072
for a connected wallet to authorize.

11
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,641
Before a payment, the workflow checks who can authorize

12
00:00:36,541 --> 00:00:39,544
it, whether the treasury has enough funds, and whether

13
00:00:39,444 --> 00:00:42,853
the category budget allows it. Those contract checks

14
00:00:42,753 --> 00:00:46,219
sit alongside the billing evidence. The implementation

15
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:49,795
is here; live payment acceptance is still pending.

16
00:00:50,053 --> 00:00:53,822
Aomi handles the transaction pipeline: prepare the contract

17
00:00:53,722 --> 00:00:57,688
call, simulate it, and ask the owner to authorize it.

18
00:00:57,588 --> 00:01:00,672
After submission, verify the receipt and payment event

19
00:01:00,572 --> 00:01:02,552
before marking the bill paid.

20
00:01:02,453 --> 00:01:05,711
The workflow's building blocks, tools, API clients,

21
00:01:05,611 --> 00:01:09,798
and prompt text, are packaged in a Rust program. Developers

22
00:01:09,698 --> 00:01:13,048
can write arbitrary logic and expose it through tools,

23
00:01:12,948 --> 00:01:16,253
with skills guiding how the agent uses them.

24
00:01:16,053 --> 00:01:21,203
A general-purpose agent framework can call APIs. Aomi

25
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:24,895
also provides cloud-hosted, protocol-agnostic contract

26
00:01:24,795 --> 00:01:28,634
access and transaction simulation and execution. The

27
00:01:28,534 --> 00:01:31,617
team defines its workflow without having to build that

28
00:01:31,517 --> 00:01:33,150
infrastructure itself.

29
00:01:32,987 --> 00:01:36,361
The frontend imports Aomi’s widget and points it at the

30
00:01:36,261 --> 00:01:39,356
app. The same workflow is now available through chat

31
00:01:39,256 --> 00:01:42,143
inside ACR’s existing interface.

32
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,588
ACR, powered by Aomi.